WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.363
On the night of the
sixteenth of November, 1957,

00:00:03.363 --> 00:00:06.115
a Wisconsin sheriff and
his officers searched

00:00:06.115 --> 00:00:08.812
a farm outside the small
town of Plainfield.

00:00:09.585 --> 00:00:11.882
They were looking for a
woman who had vanished

00:00:11.882 --> 00:00:13.782
from her hardware store that morning.

00:00:14.224 --> 00:00:16.937
In a shed on the farm, they found her.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.886
She had been shot.

00:00:19.574 --> 00:00:23.832
The farm belonged to a quiet
bachelor handyman named Ed Gein.

00:00:24.255 --> 00:00:28.521
What investigators found inside
his house shocked the country.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.908
It would later inspire
Psycho, The Texas Chain

00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:34.621
Saw Massacre and The Silence of the Lambs.

00:00:35.438 --> 00:00:39.347
According to investigators,
he admitted killing two women.

00:00:39.835 --> 00:00:42.266
He was only ever tried for one.

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:46.321
A judge found that he
had committed murder.

00:00:46.847 --> 00:00:49.215
He never spent a day in prison.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:54.431
And in 2025, more than twenty million
people watched a Netflix version of his

00:00:54.431 --> 00:00:56.063
story in a single week.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.411
Some of it never happened.

00:00:58.795 --> 00:01:02.904
This is the real case: what the
record shows, and what's legend.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:07.917
Edward Gein was born in 1906,
in La Crosse County, Wisconsin.

00:01:08.238 --> 00:01:12.878
He and his older brother, Henry, grew
up to do odd jobs around Plainfield.

00:01:13.191 --> 00:01:16.630
People there thought of
them as reliable and honest.

00:01:16.987 --> 00:01:21.323
Accounts describe their father as an
alcoholic, and their mother, Augusta,

00:01:21.323 --> 00:01:24.033
as strict, deeply
religious and domineering.

00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:28.029
She discouraged her sons from
relationships with women.

00:01:28.573 --> 00:01:33.205
In 1944, Henry died during
a brush fire near the farm.

00:01:33.869 --> 00:01:37.077
The coroner listed the
cause as asphyxiation.

00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:40.469
There was no autopsy,
and no investigation.

00:01:40.827 --> 00:01:43.993
Some writers have since
said that doesn't add up.

00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:48.234
But Ed was never charged over
Henry's death, never confessed to it,

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:51.135
and there's no direct
evidence linking him to it.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.991
A year later, his mother died.

00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:58.745
Ed lived alone on the farm, and
sealed off the rooms she had used.

00:01:59.543 --> 00:02:04.167
On the morning of Saturday the sixteenth
of November, 1957, Bernice Worden,

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.592
who ran the hardware store
in Plainfield, disappeared.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:11.012
Her son, Frank, was a deputy sheriff.

00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:15.382
When he came into the store that evening,
he found the cash register open,

00:02:15.382 --> 00:02:16.832
and blood on the floor.

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:21.819
He told investigators that Ed Gein had
been in the store the evening before,

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:24.476
and was coming back for
a gallon of antifreeze.

00:02:25.496 --> 00:02:29.678
The last sales slip his mother
wrote that day was for antifreeze.

00:02:30.281 --> 00:02:35.175
That evening, Ed Gein was arrested at
a grocery store in West Plainfield.

00:02:35.602 --> 00:02:40.049
That night, Sheriff Art Schley and
his officers searched the Gein farm.

00:02:40.448 --> 00:02:43.634
In a shed, they found
Bernice Worden's body.

00:02:44.034 --> 00:02:45.503
She had been shot.

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:50.049
Inside the house, investigators
found that Gein had robbed graves,

00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:51.713
and kept human remains.

00:02:52.252 --> 00:02:54.920
We won't describe what was found.

00:02:55.444 --> 00:02:58.012
Those details have been
retold for decades,

00:02:58.012 --> 00:03:02.415
and they belong to the people whose
graves were robbed, and to their families.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:07.878
Investigators said Gein admitted
taking remains from local graves.

00:03:08.128 --> 00:03:13.048
Investigators opened test graves to check,
and found them as he had described.

00:03:13.754 --> 00:03:17.662
Investigators said he also admitted
killing a second woman, Mary Hogan,

00:03:17.662 --> 00:03:20.605
a tavern owner who had
vanished three years earlier,

00:03:20.605 --> 00:03:23.092
though he was never
charged over her death.

00:03:23.816 --> 00:03:28.162
He said he had killed both women because
they looked like his dead mother.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:31.225
Over the years, the story grew.

00:03:31.551 --> 00:03:38.452
Only two killings are documented: Mary
Hogan in 1954, and Bernice Worden in 1957.

00:03:38.771 --> 00:03:42.649
Police checked him against
other unsolved disappearances.

00:03:42.946 --> 00:03:47.669
He was cleared of three well-known cases,
and no evidence tied him to any others.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.174
The bigger numbers you'll sometimes
hear are counts of remains,

00:03:52.174 --> 00:03:55.167
which investigators said
came mostly from graves.

00:03:55.649 --> 00:03:58.130
They are not counts of victims.

00:03:58.721 --> 00:04:01.422
And there's no evidence he ate anyone.

00:04:01.697 --> 00:04:06.967
A TIME magazine report in 1957
said he practised no cannibalism.

00:04:07.248 --> 00:04:09.329
Was he a serial killer?

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:13.182
Writers argue that it
depends on the definition.

00:04:13.545 --> 00:04:18.148
Two documented killings fall short of
the traditional threshold of three.

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:22.335
Gein was charged with the
first-degree murder of Bernice Worden,

00:04:22.335 --> 00:04:25.072
and pleaded not guilty
by reason of insanity.

00:04:25.368 --> 00:04:29.136
In early 1958 he was found
incompetent to stand trial,

00:04:29.136 --> 00:04:32.716
and committed to Central
State Hospital, at Waupun.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:36.508
Ten years later, he was found competent.

00:04:36.983 --> 00:04:43.119
In November 1968 his trial began,
before Judge Robert Gollmar, with no jury.

00:04:44.118 --> 00:04:47.937
The judge found that Gein had
committed first-degree murder.

00:04:48.414 --> 00:04:51.467
Then he found him legally
insane at the time.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.548
So he was not sent to prison.

00:04:54.999 --> 00:04:59.726
He was sent back to a mental hospital,
and never served a day behind bars.

00:05:00.538 --> 00:05:03.574
He was never tried for Mary Hogan's death.

00:05:04.338 --> 00:05:08.909
He was later moved to the Mendota
Mental Health Institute in Madison.

00:05:09.453 --> 00:05:15.135
He died there on the twenty-sixth
of July, 1984, aged seventy-seven.

00:05:15.886 --> 00:05:19.946
In March 1958, his farm
was due to be auctioned.

00:05:20.316 --> 00:05:23.528
Ten days before the sale,
the house burned down.

00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:26.888
Arson was suspected, but
no one was ever charged,

00:05:26.888 --> 00:05:29.718
and the cause was never
officially determined.

00:05:30.102 --> 00:05:34.817
Told his house had burned down,
Gein reportedly said: "Just as well."

00:05:35.571 --> 00:05:38.607
About two thousand people
came to the auction.

00:05:38.949 --> 00:05:41.975
His 1949 Ford was sold
to a carnival showman,

00:05:41.975 --> 00:05:45.950
who charged a quarter a look at
what he called the Ghoul Car.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:51.155
Even his gravestone was stolen
from Plainfield Cemetery, in 2000.

00:05:51.481 --> 00:05:53.903
And the case lived on in film.

00:05:54.213 --> 00:05:57.775
Writer Robert Bloch drew
on it for his novel Psycho,

00:05:57.775 --> 00:06:00.477
which Alfred Hitchcock filmed in 1960.

00:06:00.725 --> 00:06:03.128
Tobe Hooper said Gein was one of the

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:06.103
inspirations for The
Texas Chain Saw Massacre.

00:06:06.404 --> 00:06:09.052
And Buffalo Bill, in The
Silence of the Lambs,

00:06:09.052 --> 00:06:12.923
has been described as a composite
of several killers, Gein among them.

00:06:13.191 --> 00:06:18.153
On the third of October, 2025, Netflix
released Monster: The Ed Gein Story,

00:06:18.153 --> 00:06:19.991
starring Charlie Hunnam.

00:06:20.245 --> 00:06:23.681
In its second week, it drew
twenty point seven million views,

00:06:23.681 --> 00:06:25.527
and was number one on Netflix.

00:06:26.309 --> 00:06:30.657
Fact-checks say several scenes were
invented, including Ed killing Henry,

00:06:30.657 --> 00:06:33.243
and any link to the capture of Ted Bundy.

00:06:33.863 --> 00:06:37.152
In Plainfield, a town of
fewer than a thousand people,

00:06:37.152 --> 00:06:40.605
residents describe the new
wave of visitors as intrusive.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.982
The farm site is private property.

00:06:44.806 --> 00:06:47.421
So, here's what the record shows.

00:06:48.119 --> 00:06:52.600
According to investigators,
Ed Gein admitted killing two women.

00:06:53.035 --> 00:06:56.410
He was tried only for the
murder of Bernice Worden.

00:06:57.067 --> 00:07:01.495
A judge found he committed that murder,
and that he was legally insane.

00:07:01.959 --> 00:07:05.293
He spent the rest of his
life in state hospitals.

00:07:06.002 --> 00:07:09.056
The rest is legend: the
bigger numbers, the cannibal,

00:07:09.056 --> 00:07:11.488
and the claim that he killed his brother.
